  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kansas received $3.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state saw up 3.5% in obligations year over year, with 25,572 awards and an average award size of $145K. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in Kansas, awarding $2.3B in contracts so far. The Department of Defense obligated $640M and the Department of Transportation obligated $478M. ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor in Kansas with $2.1B in awards, followed by INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. with $392M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry by obligations at $2.1B. Fiscal history shows obligations of $2.9B in FY21, $4.2B in FY22, $3B in FY23, $3.3B in FY24, $3.6B in FY25, and $3.7B in FY26 to date. This mix of large VA health IT spending, defense and transportation buys, and concentrated vendor activity shapes where federal dollars are flowing in Kansas during the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What agencies are driving federal spending in Kansas?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is driving the most spending with $2.3B in obligations. The Department of Defense and the Department of Transportation follow with $640M and $478M respectively. Several smaller buyers include the Department of Agriculture at $144M and the Environmental Protection Agency at $53.1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate Kansas contracting?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services leads industries with $2.1B in obligations. Aircraft-related manufacturing and air-transport support are also prominent, with Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $389M and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $110M. ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. tops the vendor list with $2.1B, and INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. follows with $392M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Kansas?",
      "a": "Kansas received $3.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The FY2026 total follows fiscal-year obligations of $3.6B in FY25, $3.3B in FY24, $3B in FY23, $4.2B in FY22, and $2.9B in FY21. The state recorded 25,572 awards with an average award size of $145K and obligations were up 3.5% year over year."
    },
